74
00:11:17,519 --> 00:11:41,495
[Host] That's all for today. Japan and the United States bought yen together for the first time in fifteen years to stop the currency's historic slide, and the finance minister says more interventions may follow without hesitation. The yen strengthened to the one fifty-five range, while stocks fell as exporters' profits came under pressure. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

75
00:11:42,096 --> 00:11:44,495
[News] また明日。
